      "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nWhen `use_fused_kernels=True` and `mtp.enable=False`, the patched `_fused_GPTModel_forward` receives `labels=None` from the non-fused caller path (`gptmodel_forward_no_padding`). This causes an `AttributeError` in `linear_cross_entropy` because it tries to access `labels.shape` on `None`.\r\n\r\n**Root cause:** `patch_fused_forward` replaces `GPTModel.forward` globally, but the non-fused caller path (`gptmodel_forward_no_padding`) only passes `labels` when both `enable_mtp` and `post_process` are `True`. When MTP is disabled, the patched forward is still called without `labels`, leading to the crash.\r\n\r\n**Error traceback:**\r\n```\r\nFile \"verl/utils/kernel/linear_cross_entropy.py\", line 74, in forward\r\n    if len(labels.shape) != 1:\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape'\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nAdd a guard in `_fused_GPTModel_forward` that, when `labels is None`, falls back to standard logit computation via `model.output_layer` — matching the original `GPTModel._postprocess` behavior.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nThis fix is a minimal guard that only activates when `labels is None`. It does not affect the existing fused kernel path (which always receives labels via `fused_forward_no_padding`).\r\n\r\nFixes #5273\r\n",
