      "additions": 8,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/30cce911204105c5c7336a3aff3142b272bba9e5/verl%2Fmodels%2Fmcore%2Fmodel_forward_fused.py",
      "changes": 8,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/verl-project/verl/contents/verl%2Fmodels%2Fmcore%2Fmodel_forward_fused.py?ref=30cce911204105c5c7336a3aff3142b272bba9e5",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "verl/models/mcore/model_forward_fused.py",
      "patch": "@@ -282,6 +282,14 @@ def _fused_GPTModel_forward(\n         # When embeddings are tied, use the embedding weight\n         output_weight = model.embedding.word_embeddings.weight\n \n+    # If labels is None, we cannot use the fused kernel. This happens when the\n+    # non-fused caller path (gptmodel_forward_no_padding) invokes the model without\n+    # labels (MTP disabled), but the model's forward is still patched.\n+    # Fall back to standard logit computation matching original GPTModel._postprocess.\n+    if labels is None:\n+        logits, _ = model.output_layer(hidden_states, weight=output_weight)\n+        return logits\n+\n     logprobs, entropy = linear_cross_entropy(\n         hidden_states,\n         output_weight,",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/raw/30cce911204105c5c7336a3aff3142b272bba9e5/verl%2Fmodels%2Fmcore%2Fmodel_forward_fused.py",
      "sha": "d304cce6821394c850799e406b9734edcb425bcb",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)\n\nWhile this change correctly fixes the crash, it highlights a deeper design issue: `_fused_GPTModel_forward` has inconsistent return types. It returns a `CausalLMOutputForPPO` object when `labels` are provided, but a `torch.Tensor` when they are not.\n\nThis is brittle because different callers have different expectations:\n- `fused_forward_no_padding` expects a `CausalLMOutputForPPO` object to access attributes like `.log_probs`.\n- `gptmodel_forward_no_padding` expects a raw `torch.Tensor` to pass to `postprocess_thd_no_padding`.\n\nThe current implementation relies on an implicit contract that `fused_forward_no_padding` will always provide labels. This is fragile and can be easily broken by future changes, leading to runtime errors.\n\nA more robust solution would be to make the return type consistent. For example, `_fused_GPTModel_forward` could always return a `CausalLMOutputForPPO` object:\n```python\nif labels is None:\n    logits, _ = model.output_layer(hidden_states, weight=output_weight)\n    return CausalLMOutputForPPO(logits=logits)\n```\nThis would then require modifying `gptmodel_forward_no_padding` to extract the tensor it needs (e.g., `output_orig.logits`).\n\nWhile a larger refactor might be out of scope for this PR, this design flaw is critical for long-term maintainability and should be addressed to make the code more robust.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T02:35:35Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -282,6 +282,14 @@ def _fused_GPTModel_forward(\n         # When embeddings are tied, use the embedding weight\n         output_weight = model.embedding.word_embeddings.weight\n \n+    # If labels is None, we cannot use the fused kernel. This happens when the\n+    # non-fused caller path (gptmodel_forward_no_padding) invokes the model without\n+    # labels (MTP disabled), but the model's forward is still patched.\n+    # Fall back to standard logit computation matching original GPTModel._postprocess.\n+    if labels is None:\n+        logits, _ = model.output_layer(hidden_states, weight=output_weight)\n+        return logits",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/5332#discussion_r2810426881",
      "id": 2810426881,
      "line": 291,
      "original_line": 291,
      "path": "verl/models/mcore/model_forward_fused.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-02-16T02:35:35Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "gemini-code-assist[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Returning the logits directly here defeats the original purpose of the fused implementation.\n\nI think if you need to support MTP under the fused mode, more modifications will be required.\nAdditionally, this interface expects an output structure, so returning logits directly may cause issues.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-24T07:32:20Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -282,6 +282,14 @@ def _fused_GPTModel_forward(\n         # When embeddings are tied, use the embedding weight\n         output_weight = model.embedding.word_embeddings.weight\n \n+    # If labels is None, we cannot use the fused kernel. This happens when the\n+    # non-fused caller path (gptmodel_forward_no_padding) invokes the model without\n+    # labels (MTP disabled), but the model's forward is still patched.\n+    # Fall back to standard logit computation matching original GPTModel._postprocess.\n+    if labels is None:\n+        logits, _ = model.output_layer(hidden_states, weight=output_weight)\n+        return logits",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/5332#discussion_r2845055463",
      "id": 2845055463,
